  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 125 PM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nWarm and dry conditions are expected across the majority of South \nTexas this week, with the exception being parts of the Victoria \nCrossroads. Potential Tropical Cyclone 5 is expected to move west-\nnorthwest to northwest towards the Upper Texas Coast. Locally, we \nare not expected to see any impacts from this system with the \nexception of an isolated to scattered shower or two across parts of \nthe Victoria Crossroads. What we will see are hot conditions. Warm \nand moist air will promote heat index values around 110 degrees each \nafternoon with a moderate to extreme heat risk threat. If working \noutdoors, make sure to take frequent breaks and hydrate adequately. \n\nMore heat safety information can be found at weather.gov/heat",
